course: dictionary
lesson: 4406
title: A word from the cold sea
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can learn a lot about a word from the sentences around it. «Narwhals dive to about 1,500 metres or more under the Arctic sea ice to hunt halibut, squid and shrimps.» Squid and shrimps are sea creatures that narwhals eat, so halibut must be a sea creature that narwhals eat too.
explain: The sentence also tells you where it lives. The Arctic sea ice is frozen, so halibut live in cold water. A dictionary says a halibut is a very large flat fish from cold northern seas, such as the North Atlantic and North Pacific. Check it by putting the meaning into the sentence: «Narwhals hunt very large flat fish from cold northern seas» still makes sense.
explain: Halibut is also a food word. A halibut steak is a thick slice of halibut, and it can be grilled, put in fish and chips, or baked in a fish pie. The same word can name a living fish in a science lesson and a meal on a plate, so look at the words around it to see which one is meant.
fact: A halibut is a very large flat fish.
fact: Halibut live in cold northern seas, such as the North Atlantic and North Pacific.
fact: In science, halibut are flatfish: both eyes are on one side of the head, and they lie on the sea floor.
fact: As food, halibut is a white fish. It can be grilled, served as halibut steak, or used in fish and chips or fish pie.
fact: Halibut fishing is important in Canada and Alaska. Phrases to remember: halibut steak, Atlantic halibut.
exercise: «Narwhals dive under the Arctic sea ice to hunt halibut, squid and shrimps.» What is a halibut? | A small green plant | A thick layer of ice on a river | *A very large flat fish from cold northern seas | A bird that flies over the sea
exercise: In science, a halibut lies on the sea floor. Which feature makes a halibut a flatfish? | It has a shell like a snail | It has no fins at all | It can fly short distances above the waves | *Both of its eyes are on one side of its head
exercise: Which of these would you most likely find on a menu? | Halibut hiking boots | A halibut bicycle helmet | *Grilled halibut steak | Halibut and sunflower bedroom curtains
test: Where do halibut live? | Mountain lakes high above the clouds | *Cold northern seas, such as the North Atlantic | Warm tropical rivers | Hot desert sands far from any sea
test: Which phrase is a kind of fish dish? | Halibut blanket | *Halibut steak | Halibut tree | Halibut bus stop
exam: Which sentence about halibut is correct? | *A halibut is a very large flat fish from cold northern seas | A halibut is a tiny bird that lives in deserts | A halibut is a type of sea ice that narwhals dive under | A halibut is a tall tree found in tropical forests
